Just had the same issue (v34).

I tested a lot of things.

The exact same parameters were working with silent: false and not working with silent: true. And that, even if the window was hidden or not.

I fixed this with a setTimeout on 2 things :
- First, wait a bit before closing the window, to be sure the content you transfer to the printer is fully known by the printer.
- Secondly and most important for silent: true, was to not call print() too fast after the `did-finish-load` event.

I put a lot of seconds to be sure that would work, maybe that can vary between networks and printers : 

```ts
const win = new BrowserWindow({
  show: false,
});

const b64 = `data:application/pdf;base64,${pdf}`;
win.loadURL(b64);

win.webContents.on('did-finish-load', () => {
    setTimeout(() => {
        win.webContents.print({
            silent: true,
            color: true,
            copies: 1,
            pageSize: 'A4',
            printBackground: false,
            collate: true,
            margins: {
                marginType: 'default'
            },
            duplexMode: 'simplex',
            dpi: {
                horizontal: 600,
                vertical: 600
            },
            landscape: false,
            pagesPerSheet: 1,
        }, (success, failureReason) => {
            if(!success) {
                console.log(failureReason);
                win.close();
                return;
            }

            console.info('Document printed');

            setTimeout(() => {
                win.close();
            }, 5000); // maybe a fix (to be sure it does not close too fast)
        });
    }, 3000); // fix
});
```

I tried with different events to try to avoid using a `setTimeout` (`dom-ready`, `did-frame-finish-load`) but all were firing before `did-finish-load` event and printed blank sheet.

